ated among customers with the lowest average balances. A fee designed as a deterrent has become a recurring charge falling on the customers least able to absorb it. My cousin once paid four overdraft fees in a single week, which shows how quickly they add up."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","$L29","ev-g1",{"question":{"id":"ev-g1","type":"multiple-choice","question":"Which sentence provides the strongest support for the author's claim?","passageId":"ev-guided-fees","choices":["Overdraft fees should be capped by regulation.","Banking data has repeatedly shown that a small share of account holders pay the large majority of all overdraft fees collected.","A fee designed as a deterrent has become a recurring charge.","My cousin once paid four overdraft fees in a single week."],"correctAnswer":1,"hint":"One of these sentences is the claim itself, one is an interpretation, and one is a single story. Only one brings outside data.","explanation":"Support has to come from outside the claim. The banking data is the only sentence offering verifiable, repeated evidence about a pattern across many customers.","choiceRationales":["This is the claim. A claim cannot support itself.","Correct. Repeated data about a population is relevant, sufficient, and representative.","An interpretation of the data rather than evidence in its own right.","A single anecdote. It illustrates the problem vividly but proves nothing about the pattern."],"skill":"evidence","difficulty":"Developing"},"number":1}]]}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","section",null,{"id":"practice","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"Practice"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"Practice on a full passage"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"A longer passage with several questions. Check each answer as you go."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":["$undefined",[["$","article","ev-practice-transit",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white shadow-sm","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-eng-navy-100 px-4 py-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Free Fares"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-eng-teal-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-eng-teal-800","children":"Argument"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-eng-navy-400","children":[250," words"]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-4 py-5 sm:px-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":1}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The city should eliminate fares on its bus system."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Fare collection is expensive in ways that are easy to overlook. Fare boxes must be maintained, revenue must be counted and transported, and fare enforcement requires staff. In some smaller systems, these costs consume a meaningful share of the revenue the fares bring in."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Free fares also speed up service. Boarding is the slowest part of a bus route, and passengers who do not need to pay board through any door. One transit agency that removed fares on a downtown route reported that average trip times fell by roughly nine percent."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Ridership rises as well. Every system that has tried free fares has seen ridership grow, in some cases dramatically."}]]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":5}],["$","span",null,{"children":"A friend of mine stopped driving entirely after her city made buses free, which shows that people will change their habits when the barrier is removed."}]]}],["$","p","5",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":6}],"$L2a"]}]]}],"$undefined","$L2b"]}]]}]],"$L2c"]}]]}]
